# Firebase service account (server-side only, never exposed to the browser).
#
# Local development:
#   1. Minify your serviceAccountKey.json to a single line:
#        cat serviceAccountKey.json | tr -d '\n'
#   2. Paste the result as the value below. Keep the literal \n sequences
#      inside the private_key exactly as they appear in the minified output.
#
# Netlify (production):
#   - Create an environment variable named FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT in
#     Netlify Dashboard > Site configuration > Environment variables.
#   - Paste the SAME minified single-line string as the value.
#
# The server code normalizes line breaks before JSON.parse, so the same
# string works on both macOS (local) and Netlify (Linux).
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n",...}